# 𝓔𝓷𝓬𝓸𝓭𝓮‑2025
A concise, elegant project README with clear scope, tech stack, and usage.

## ✨ Overview
This project aims to provide a lightweight, extensible toolkit for encoding/transforming data streams and file formats with an emphasis on performance, clarity, and testability.

## 🎯 Project Scope
- Core encoding/decoding primitives and pipelines
- Pluggable adapters for file formats and protocols
- Simple CLI and library APIs for embedding in other projects
- CI tests, benchmarks, and examples

## 🧩 Technologies Used
- ⚡ Rust — core engine for speed and safety  
- 🔧 Node.js/TypeScript — CLI and tooling glue  
- 🧪 GitHub Actions — CI & automated tests  
- 📦 TOML / JSON — configuration formats

## 🚀 Quick Start
Clone, build, run tests:
```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd repo
# build (example for Rust)
cargo build --release
# run tests
cargo test
```

## 🧭 Usage (example)
- Library: import the crate/module and call Encoder::new(...)  
- CLI: ./encode2025 --input file.bin --format json --output out.json

